{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.PhaseBoundaryVariety","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.PhaseBoundaryVariety","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhaseBoundaryVariety","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhaseBoundaryVariety","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/phase-boundary-variety.lean#L36-L50","doc":"**Phase-boundary variety is measure-zero.**\n\nThe full variety `ℬ` is the finite union of the pairwise-equality\nloci (each a polynomial zero-set, see\n`phaseBoundaryLocus_eq_zeroSet`) with the shadow-price vanishing\nloci. A finite union of codimension-≥1 Zariski-closed sets is\nmeasure-zero; the proof needs the algebraic-variety / Lebesgue\nmeasure API for the base ring `Q`, deferred here. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:phase-boundary-variety","label":"prop:phase-boundary-variety","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/phase-boundary-variety.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.phaseBoundaryLocus_eq_zeroSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.phaseBoundaryLocus_eq_zeroSet","kind":"theorem","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/phase-boundary-variety.lean#L19-L34","doc":"The pairwise-equality locus\n`ℬ_{λ₁,λ₂} = {q : y_{λ₁}²(q) = y_{λ₂}²(q)}` is cut out by the\nsingle polynomial equation `y_{λ₁}²(q) - y_{λ₂}²(q) = 0`, hence it\nequals the zero-set of `y_{λ₁}² - y_{λ₂}²` — the algebraic content\nof \"Zariski-closed of codimension ≥ 1\".\n\n(The downstream measure-zero claim for the finite union `ℬ`\nadditionally requires the variety / measure API for `Q`; it is\nrecorded as `phaseBoundary_measure_zero` below.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}